-- title:
--   The complete source-band bank survives preservation of its retained prefix
-- statement:
--   Let $\mu,\nu$ be integer memories, $f_L,f_R$ source-value functions, and $b,N_L,N_R,g,h,J,c,o,E$ natural layout parameters, with integer residue parameter $p$ and shift $z$. Suppose $\mu$ stores the source-band bank based at $b$: its five-cell header, every common-band source catalog, and the occurrence table based at $o$. Let $T$ be the local schedule length and $F$ the bank's final allocation address. Assume
--   $$o+T^J J\le b,\qquad F\le E,\qquad \forall a<E,\ \nu(a)=\mu(a).$$
--   Then
--   $$\operatorname{Stored}(\mu,f_L,f_R,b,N_L,N_R,g,h,J,c,o,p,z)
--   \Longrightarrow\operatorname{Stored}(\nu,f_L,f_R,b,N_L,N_R,g,h,J,c,o,p,z).$$
--
--   This preserves both the source-stage catalogs and the physical occurrence labels needed to select them later.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SourceBandBankData.lean#L34-L50

